jobs.description:
Receives incoming documents for the Office of the District Engineer.
Sorts, classifies and distributes documents to concern section;
Answers phone calls, assists visitors/clients and refers their queries to concerned staff/section;
Arrange regular cleaning, maintenance services and takes charge of the proper care of the assigned vehicle to the section;
Performs minor repairs of the vehicle when necessary.;
Performs other tasks as may be assigned by the immediate supervisor.
- Preferably with relevant experience on basic admin works.

1. Assist in the preparation of payrolls and other personnel benefits of the officials and employees of the Ministry;
2. Assist in the preparation of needed documents for appointment of both regular and job order personnel;
3. Maintains and updates personnel files;
4. Performs other related functions as may be directed/assigned by the immediate supervisor.

